---

# 5. The “prompt itself” architecture

Manual prompts become compiled artifacts.

## Inputs

```text
Beads issue
GitHub issue
Slack request
PM task
Agency workflow node
CLI command
```

## Normalized object

```ts
type TaskSpec = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  intent:
    | "bugfix"
    | "feature"
    | "refactor"
    | "review"
    | "test"
    | "deploy"
    | "research"
    | "support"
    | "security";

  repo: string;
  branchPolicy: "new_branch" | "worktree" | "existing_branch";
  targetPaths: string[];
  forbiddenPaths: string[];

  acceptanceCriteria: string[];
  verification: VerificationPlan;

  requiredArtifacts: string[];
  approvalGates: ApprovalGate[];

  source: {
    kind: "beads" | "github" | "slack" | "pm" | "agency" | "manual";
    externalId?: string;
  };
};
```

## Compiler output

```ts
type InstructionBundle = {
  id: string;
  taskId: string;
  agentId: string;

  runtime:
    | "claude_code"
    | "codex"
    | "recoder_code"
    | "opencode"
    | "qwen_code"
    | "gemini_cli"
    | "browser_agent";

  goal: string;
  renderedPrompt: string;

  loadedSources: Array<{
    kind:
      | "AGENTS.md"
      | "CLAUDE.md"
      | "codex"
      | "skill"
      | "beads"
      | "git_nexus"
      | "pal"
      | "memory"
      | "policy"
      | "context7";
    pathOrRef: string;
    sha256?: string;
  }>;

  allowedTools: string[];
  deniedTools: string[];
  workLocks: string[];
  approvalGates: ApprovalGate[];
  verificationCommands: string[];
  artifactRequirements: string[];

  provenance: {
    compilerVersion: string;
    compiledAt: string;
  };
};
```

## Flow

```text
Beads issue #123
  ↓
TaskSpec
  ↓
Git Nexus says: likely files, owners, tests, risks
  ↓
PAL says: use Claude for implementation, Codex for review, Playwright for verify
  ↓
MCP says: available tools and permissions
  ↓
Policy says: auth changes require approval
  ↓
Compiler renders Claude/Codex-specific InstructionBundle
  ↓
A2A dispatches task
  ↓
Agent runs through MCP + sandbox
  ↓
Artifacts and verification attach
  ↓
Beads/GitHub/PM update
```

This is the replacement for manual prompting.

---

# 6. How each OSS piece plugs in

## Beads

Beads should be the **repo-local task graph**.

Use it for:

```text
task dependencies
local issue queue
branch/session continuity
offline work
agent handoff notes
small implementation tickets
```

Mapping:

```text
.beads issue
  ↔ Recoder TaskSpec

.beads dependency
  ↔ Task dependency / workflow edge

.beads status
  ↔ Recoder task status

.beads comments
  ↔ Run summary / artifact references

.beads tags
  ↔ intent, runtime, priority, risk
```

Folder/package:

```text
packages/beads-adapter/
├── src/
│   ├── beads-client.ts
│   ├── beads-parser.ts
│   ├── task-spec-mapper.ts
│   ├── sync-to-recoder.ts
│   ├── sync-from-recoder.ts
│   └── index.ts
```

Commands:

```bash
pnpm beads:sync
pnpm beads:task:create
pnpm beads:task:status
```

Example bead metadata:

```yaml
id: bd_123
title: "Fix Recoder agent run artifact streaming"
intent: bugfix
runtime_hint: claude_code
review_runtime: codex
risk: medium
target_paths:
  - packages/agent-runtimes/**
  - apps/agent-gateway/**
verify:
  - pnpm check-types
  - pnpm test
depends_on:
  - bd_117
```

---

## Git Nexus

Git Nexus should be the **repo intelligence engine**.

Use it before the prompt compiler, not after.

It should produce:

```text
RepoMap
PackageMap
OwnershipMap
DependencyGraph
ChangedFileRisk
TestTargetMap
ImpactReport
ContextPack
```

Package:

```text
packages/git-nexus/
├── src/
│   ├── repo-indexer.ts
│   ├── dependency-graph.ts
│   ├── ownership-map.ts
│   ├── test-target-map.ts
│   ├── impact-report.ts
│   ├── context-pack.ts
│   └── mcp-server.ts
```

MCP tools:

```text
recoder.git_nexus.search_code
recoder.git_nexus.get_package_map
recoder.git_nexus.get_owners
recoder.git_nexus.get_related_tests
recoder.git_nexus.impact_report
recoder.git_nexus.context_pack
```

Compiler use:

```text
TaskSpec target_paths
  ↓
Git Nexus impact report
  ↓
compiler includes:
  - relevant files
  - related tests
  - package boundaries
  - owners
  - risky paths
  - likely verification commands
```

This avoids dumping huge repo context into Claude/Codex.

---

## PAL

Treat PAL as the **planner / agent team layer**.

If your internal meaning of PAL differs, keep the name but this role is still needed.

PAL should answer:

```text
Which agent should do this?
Which agent should review?
Should this run in sandbox?
Does this need browser verification?
Does this need human approval?
Which skills should load?
Which MCP tools should be allowed?
```

Package:

```text
packages/pal/
├── src/
│   ├── planner.ts
│   ├── agent-team.ts
│   ├── routing-policy.ts
│   ├── task-intent-classifier.ts
│   ├── skill-selector.ts
│   ├── runtime-selector.ts
│   ├── approval-estimator.ts
│   └── index.ts
```

PAL output:

```ts
type PALPlan = {
  taskId: string;
  primaryRuntime: "claude_code" | "codex" | "recoder_code";
  reviewerRuntime?: "codex" | "claude_code" | "recoder_code";
  browserVerification: boolean;
  sandbox: "daytona" | "e2b" | "local_container";
  skills: string[];
  mcpTools: string[];
  approvalGates: ApprovalGate[];
  risk: "low" | "medium" | "high";
};
```

PAL does not execute. It plans.

---

## MCP

MCP is the **tool/context layer**.

MCP provides a standard way for LLM apps to share context, expose tools/capabilities, and build composable workflows over JSON-RPC with hosts, clients, and servers. ([modelcontextprotocol.io][4]) MCP servers expose resources, prompts, and tools; in Recoder terms, that maps perfectly to repo context, prompt templates, and executable actions. ([modelcontextprotocol.io][4])

Recoder MCP servers:

```text
recoder.tasks
recoder.runs
recoder.artifacts
recoder.approvals
recoder.memory
recoder.git_nexus
recoder.beads
recoder.github
recoder.repo
recoder.browser
recoder.preview
recoder.deploy
recoder.billing
recoder.logs
recoder.oss
```

Package:

```text
packages/agent-mcp/
├── src/
│   ├── host/
│   │   ├── mcp-host.ts
│   │   ├── session-manager.ts
│   │   ├── tool-router.ts
│   │   └── registry.ts
│   ├── servers/
│   │   ├── tasks-server.ts
│   │   ├── artifacts-server.ts
│   │   ├── approvals-server.ts
│   │   ├── memory-server.ts
│   │   ├── git-nexus-server.ts
│   │   ├── beads-server.ts
│   │   ├── browser-server.ts
│   │   └── oss-server.ts
│   └── policy/
│       ├── tool-risk.ts
│       └── permission-check.ts
```

Every MCP call must go through policy:

```text
agent → MCP tool call → Recoder policy → allow / deny / approval → audit event
```

---

## A2A

A2A should be the **agent/task wire layer**.

The A2A spec defines tasks with status, artifacts, and history; tasks can stream status/artifact updates and terminate as completed, failed, canceled, or rejected. ([a2a-protocol.org][5]) It also supports authenticated extended Agent Cards and Agent Card signatures, which Recoder should use for trusted agent capability discovery. ([a2a-protocol.org][5])

Use A2A for:

```text
agent discovery
agent capabilities
task send
task claim
task status
run streaming
artifact updates
cancellation
agent-to-agent handoff
```

Recoder extensions:

```text
SignedTaskEnvelope
InstructionBundleRef
PolicyDecisionRef
WorkLockRef
ApprovalGateRef
VerificationPlanRef
MemoryCandidateRef
```

Package:

```text
packages/a2a-sdk/
├── src/
│   ├── schemas/
│   │   ├── agent-card.ts
│   │   ├── task-envelope.ts
│   │   ├── signed-envelope.ts
│   │   ├── artifact.ts
│   │   └── errors.ts
│   ├── client/
│   ├── server/
│   ├── signing/
│   └── index.ts
```

---

## Claude Code

Claude Code is the **deep implementation runtime**.

Use it for:

```text
large repo changes
multi-file debugging
refactors
skills-driven workflows
long reasoning
implementation from TaskSpec
```

Files:

```text
CLAUDE.md
.claude/rules/
.claude/skills/recoder-platform/
.claude/settings.json
```

Root `CLAUDE.md`:

```md
@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code specific rules

- Prefer Recoder TaskSpec over freeform prompts.
- Use Recoder MCP tools for tasks, artifacts, approvals, memory, and Git Nexus.
- Use project skills for repeatable procedures.
- Do not silently write memory; create memory candidates.
- Treat instructions as guidance. Policy is enforced by hooks/server-side Recoder.
```

Skills:

```text
.claude/skills/recoder-platform/
├── SKILL.md
├── task-spec-template.yaml
├── verification-playbook.md
├── delivery-summary-template.md
├── memory-candidate-template.json
└── scripts/
    ├── load-task.ts
    ├── emit-artifact.ts
    └── verify-run.ts
```

---

## Codex

Codex is the **parallel investigation / patch / review / test runtime**.

Use it for:

```text
PR review
small patches
test generation
parallel repo investigation
risk review
verification
```

Files:

```text
AGENTS.md
.codex/AGENTS.md
.codex/config.toml
.codex/hooks/
```

Codex hooks should enforce:

```text
no forbidden path write
work lock required
secret scan
artifact required before stop
verification required before complete
memory candidates only, no silent memory write
```

Codex `PreToolUse` can intercept Bash, patch/file edit operations, and MCP tool calls, but OpenAI’s docs explicitly describe it as a guardrail rather than a complete enforcement boundary, so Recoder must also enforce server-side policy. ([OpenAI Developers][6])

---

