# 9. Runtime flow

## Create task

```text
User creates task in PM
or Beads issue exists
or Slack asks agent
or GitHub issue assigned
```

## Recoder normalizes

```text
Input → TaskSpec
TaskSpec gets stable id
TaskSpec stored in DB
TaskSpec linked to Beads/GitHub/Slack source
```

## Beads contributes graph

```text
dependencies
blocked-by
related tasks
local notes
previous artifacts
```

## Git Nexus contributes repo context

```text
likely files
package owners
related tests
impact report
risk paths
dependency graph
```

## PAL plans

```text
primary runtime: Claude Code
review runtime: Codex
browser verification: Playwright MCP
sandbox: Daytona
approval: auth files require human
skills: recoder-platform, code-review, verify-preview
```

## Compiler renders

```text
Claude InstructionBundle
Codex ReviewBundle
Playwright VerificationBundle
```

## A2A/MCP run

```text
A2A dispatches task
MCP exposes tools
Hooks enforce policy
Artifacts stream
```

## Finish

```text
verification result
delivery summary
PR/preview
approval
memory candidate
Beads/GitHub/PM update
```

---

# 10. State machine

```text
draft
  ↓
created
  ↓
indexed_by_git_nexus
  ↓
planned_by_pal
  ↓
compiled
  ↓
ready_for_agent
  ↓
claimed
  ↓
work_lock_acquired
  ↓
running
  ↓
needs_input ───────────────┐
  ↓                         │
waiting_for_approval ───────┤
  ↓                         │
approved                    │
  ↓                         │
verifying                   │
  ↓                         │
delivering                  │
  ↓                         │
completed ◄─────────────────┘

terminal:
failed
cancelled
rejected
expired
```

Each transition writes:

```text
RunEvent
AuditLog
Artifact if applicable
Beads/GitHub/PM sync if applicable
Trace span
```

---

# 11. Security model

Use three layers.

```text
1. Instructions
   AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .codex/AGENTS.md, skills

2. Runtime guardrails
   Claude settings/hooks
   Codex hooks
   MCP tool permissions

3. Recoder server enforcement
   policy engine
   work locks
   signed envelopes
   approval gates
   artifact requirements
```

Never rely on prompts alone.

Policy decisions:

```ts
type PolicyDecision = {
  decision: "allow" | "deny" | "require_approval";
  reason: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidence: {
    agentId: string;
    taskId: string;
    action: string;
    target?: string;
  };
};
```

Critical gates:

```text
file.write
shell.command
mcp.tool.call
secret.read
network.request
memory.write
artifact.publish
branch.push
pull_request.open
preview.deploy
production.deploy
billing.change
auth.change
```

