## D. Protocol layer

| Component         | Path                                                                             | Agent OS role                                  |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| MCP               | `mcp`, `.mcp.json`                                                               | Tool/resource/prompt protocol.                 |
| A2A SDK/contracts | `packages`, `shared`, `.env.a2a.workers.example`, `tools/a2a-interop` if present | Agent-to-agent task/message/artifact protocol. |
| WebSocket bridge  | `docker-backend`, `mcp`, likely bridge routes                                    | Local agent connection and streaming.          |
| Inbox hook        | `.claude` commit mentions A2A standard server + inbox hook                       | Agent message ingress.                         |

MCP should be your tool/context layer. The MCP spec defines tools, resources, prompts, roots, sampling, and related protocol primitives for connecting models to external systems. ([Model Context Protocol][3]) A2A should be your agent/task transport layer, because it defines agent cards, tasks, messages, status, artifacts, and streaming task updates. ([A2A Protocol][4])

Target contract:

```text
McpServer
McpHost
A2AAgent
A2ATaskTransport
SignedEnvelope
```

