# 5. Component-by-component integration plan

## 5.1 Beads

Use Beads as the local/offline task graph.

```text
.beads issue
  → TaskSpec

.beads dependency
  → Task dependency

.beads status
  → Recoder task status

.beads comments
  → Run summaries / artifact links

.beads tags
  → intent, risk, runtime hints
```

Create:

```text
packages/beads-adapter/
├── src/
│   ├── beads-client.ts
│   ├── beads-parser.ts
│   ├── task-spec-mapper.ts
│   ├── sync-to-recoder.ts
│   ├── sync-from-recoder.ts
│   └── index.ts
```

MCP tools:

```text
recoder.beads.list
recoder.beads.get
recoder.beads.create
recoder.beads.update_status
recoder.beads.link_artifact
recoder.beads.add_dependency
```

---

## 5.2 Git Nexus

Use Git Nexus as repo intelligence.

It should produce:

```text
RepoMap
PackageMap
OwnershipMap
DependencyGraph
RelatedTests
ChangedFileRisk
ContextPack
ImpactReport
```

Create:

```text
packages/git-nexus/
├── src/
│   ├── repo-indexer.ts
│   ├── dependency-graph.ts
│   ├── ownership-map.ts
│   ├── test-target-map.ts
│   ├── impact-report.ts
│   ├── context-pack.ts
│   └── mcp-server.ts
```

MCP tools:

```text
recoder.git_nexus.search_code
recoder.git_nexus.get_context_pack
recoder.git_nexus.get_related_tests
recoder.git_nexus.get_impact_report
recoder.git_nexus.get_owners
recoder.git_nexus.get_package_graph
```

Instruction compiler use:

```text
TaskSpec.targetPaths
  → Git Nexus ContextPack
  → fewer tokens, better context, better tests
```

---

## 5.3 PAL

Use PAL as the planner and agent-team router.

PAL should answer:

```text
Which runtime should do the work?
Which runtime should review?
Which skills should load?
Which tools are needed?
Which sandbox is needed?
Which approval gates are required?
Which verification path is enough?
```

Create:

```text
packages/pal/
├── src/
│   ├── planner.ts
│   ├── task-intent-classifier.ts
│   ├── runtime-selector.ts
│   ├── skill-selector.ts
│   ├── tool-grant-selector.ts
│   ├── sandbox-selector.ts
│   ├── approval-estimator.ts
│   ├── risk-model.ts
│   └── index.ts
```

Output:

```ts
type PALPlan = {
  primaryRuntime: "claude_code" | "codex" | "recoder_code" | "opencode";
  reviewRuntime?: "codex" | "claude_code" | "recoder_code";
  sandbox: "none" | "daytona" | "e2b" | "local_container";
  skills: string[];
  mcpTools: string[];
  approvalGates: ApprovalGate[];
  verification: VerificationPlan;
  risk: "low" | "medium" | "high";
};
```

---

## 5.4 MCP

Use MCP as the tool/resource/prompt layer.

Create a Recoder MCP host and many Recoder MCP servers:

```text
packages/agent-mcp/
├── src/
│   ├── host/
│   │   ├── mcp-host.ts
│   │   ├── session-manager.ts
│   │   ├── server-registry.ts
│   │   └── tool-router.ts
│   ├── servers/
│   │   ├── tasks-server.ts
│   │   ├── runs-server.ts
│   │   ├── artifacts-server.ts
│   │   ├── approvals-server.ts
│   │   ├── memory-server.ts
│   │   ├── beads-server.ts
│   │   ├── git-nexus-server.ts
│   │   ├── browser-server.ts
│   │   ├── preview-server.ts
│   │   ├── deploy-server.ts
│   │   ├── logs-server.ts
