# 7. The real “prompt itself” pipeline using everything

```text
1. Task source
   - Beads
   - GitHub
   - Slack
   - Chatwoot
   - PM
   - Agency workflow
   - manual user request

2. Normalize
   - TaskSpec

3. Task graph
   - Beads dependencies
   - task priority
   - blockers
   - related work

4. Repo context
   - Git Nexus context pack
   - package graph
   - owners
   - tests
   - risk paths

5. Plan
   - PAL chooses agent team
   - PAL chooses runtime
   - PAL chooses skills
   - PAL chooses sandbox
   - PAL chooses approvals

6. Tool layer
   - MCP grants
   - browser tools
   - deploy tools
   - memory tools
   - GitHub tools
   - Beads tools

7. Policy
   - work locks
   - path rules
   - secret rules
   - production gates
   - auth/billing gates

8. Compile
   - AGENTS.md
   - CLAUDE.md
   - .codex/AGENTS.md
   - .claude/rules
   - skills
   - memory refs
   - Context7 docs
   - verification plan
   - tool grants

9. Dispatch
   - A2A task envelope
   - Claude Code / Codex / Recoder Code / other runtime

10. Execute
   - MCP tools
   - sandbox
   - browser verification
   - repo edits

11. Verify
   - tests
   - build
   - Playwright
   - preview
   - security scan

12. Deliver
   - artifact
   - PR
   - preview URL
   - approval
   - Beads/GitHub/PM update

13. Remember
   - memory candidate
   - evidence
   - review
   - accepted memory
```

---

